# What never enters the gov-install build context — BuildKit reads this file, next to the Dockerfile, in
# preference to any .dockerignore at the context root.
#
# DENY-ONLY, deliberately. The context is either the repo root (`build.context: repo`, which `local` needs) or
# site/ itself, and one file has to be right for both. An allow-list (`*` then `!site`) would empty the build
# the moment the context is site/, because there is no site/ inside site/.
#
# site/.dockerignore stays for builders that do not read a Dockerfile-specific ignore file (podman on the deploy
# agent, depending on version). There the context is a fresh checkout, which has none of this anyway.
.git
**/node_modules
**/lib
**/dist
**/*.tgz
